  "footnote": "All major courses require a letter grade of C- or better; transferred Linguistics credits require B- or better. Declaration requires LING 1101 and at least one other Foundation Course with B- or higher (the page does not clearly say whether this threshold applies to both). Substitutions require an advisor petition and director of undergraduate studies approval. Optional honors requires overall GPA 3.3 and major GPA 3.5, with provisional admission possible; apply by the start of senior fall. Honors adds a thesis, typically eight credits over two semesters: LING 4493 and LING 4491, then required LING 4494 and LING 4492, an oral defense, a deposited thesis, and an expected year-end presentation. Honors is reviewed by a departmental committee.",
